  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova&apos;s major trade union, the National Trade Union Confederation of Moldova (CNSM), has made significant progress in management and organization. CNSM is the voice of workers in regular social dialogue, particularly through the National Commission for Consultations and Collective Bargaining. The union faces challenges as existing structures are not fully engaged in all relevant labour policy negotiations. The ILO supports CNSM by enhancing trade union engagement in labour policies and increasing the impact of social dialogue, focusing on formalizing the informal economy. 
Moldova aims at EU integration. ILO supports CNSM to promote social dialogue and International Labour Standards in this political context.   
The ILO has collaborated with Moldova to develop the National Programme to tackle Undeclared Work, ensuring CNSM&apos;s active involvement in its implementation. The union provides inputs on promoting formalization through increased coverage of collective bargaining, incentives for SMEs and workers, social security systems, and upskilling for vulnerable workers. 
The ILO aims to increase trade union influence on national and sectoral formalization policies and programs. CNSM will develop national policy inputs on formalizing informal economy workers, present them in the national social dialogue platform, and lead nationwide campaigns to promote these policies and highlight the benefits of formalization. Additionally, the ILO supports CNSM on just transition, based on ACTRAV&#x2019;s User&#x2019;s manual to the ILO&#x2019;s Guidelines for a Just Transition Towards Environmentally Sustainable Economies and Societies for All, and best practices in Europe. 
Through these efforts, the ILO contributes to increased social and economic opportunities for workers in Moldova.</narrative>
  </description>
